<section class="shell band" id="emdria">
  <h2>What EMDRIA asks for, and where these hours fit</h2>
  <p class="intro-wide">Certification is not a course you finish. It is a set of conditions
  EMDRIA checks when you apply, and consultation is the one that takes longest to accumulate.
  Here is the shape of it, so you can see what you already have.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption class="vh">EMDRIA Certified Therapist requirements</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>What EMDRIA requires</th><th>The detail</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Full licensure</td><td>Licensed for independent practice in your state</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Basic training</td><td>An EMDRIA-approved EMDR Basic Training, completed in full</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Two years</td><td>In your licensed field</td></tr>
        <tr><td>50 sessions, 25 clients</td><td>EMDR sessions conducted after Basic Training</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>20 consultation hours</strong></td><td>At least 10 individual, with at
        least 5 from a full Approved Consultant rather than a Consultant in Training. Within the
        five years before you apply.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>12 EMDRIA Credits</td><td>Continuing education earned after Basic Training</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Letters</td><td>One from an Approved Consultant, plus two from peers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="intro-wide">Reem is a full EMDRIA Approved Consultant, so hours with her count
  toward the whole twenty and toward the five that a Consultant in Training cannot supply.
  Certification is granted for two years and renewed. These are EMDRIA's criteria rather than
  this practice's, and they change, so
  <a href="https://www.emdria.org/emdr-training/emdr-certification-2/" rel="noopener">check the
  current list with EMDRIA</a><span class="vh"> (opens in a new tab)</span> before you plan
  around them.</p>
  <h3>If you are going further</h3>
  <p class="intro-wide">Consultant in Training is the next step after certification, and it
  also needs 20 hours, at least 10 individual, of consultation on your own consulting. Reem
  takes consultants in training as well as therapists working toward certification.</p>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Who tends to book this</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div>
        <h3>The therapist accumulating hours</h3>
        <p>You are working toward certification and need individual hours from a full Approved
        Consultant. Bring live cases; the hours and the help are the same hours.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The one whose processing keeps collapsing</h3>
        <p>Preparation looks adequate, then phase four floods or flatlines. Usually a protective
        part was never consulted, and the fix is upstream of where it went wrong.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The one trained years ago</h3>
        <p>You did Basic Training, used it for a while, and drifted. Common, and a fine place to
        start. We rebuild from the preparation phases rather than from the manual.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The consultant in training</h3>
        <p>You are certified and building toward Approved Consultant. What you need is
        consultation on your consulting, which is a different conversation from case work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band">
  <h2>What an hour looks like</h2>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p>Bring a case, ideally one that is not going well. Recordings are welcome and not
      required. Most of the hour is spent on the part of the work before reprocessing, because
      that is where most of the trouble starts.</p>
      <p>Your own responses in the room are treated as clinical information rather than as
      something to manage privately. If a client's material is doing something to your nervous
      system, that is data about the case as well as about you.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Individual hours are scheduled as you need them rather than on a fixed rota, which
      suits accumulating twenty of them around a full caseload.</p>
      <p>The first conversation is free and exists to check fit. If what you need is closer to
      supervision, training or a different consultant, that is a useful thing to find out in
      thirty minutes.</p>
